etts. Diversified Healthcare Trust was established in 1998 and is incorporated in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher J. Bilotto | President, CEO & Managing Trustee | Age 47 | Compensation: $3,523 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Diversified Healthcare Trust is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.7B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $166M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 16.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 10% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 30% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Diversified Healthcare Trust (NASDAQ:DHC) Releases Earnings Results, Misses Expectations By $0.06 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/diversified-healthcare-trust-nasdaqdhc-releases-earnings-results-misses-expectations-by-0-06-eps.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793800646.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Diversified Healthcare Trust (DHC) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: SHOP NOI Surges 50% as ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/diversified-healthcare-trust-dhc-q3-010713407.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793754433.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Diversified Healthcare Trust (DHC) Stock Dips Despite Strong Q3 Results","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nasdaq-dhc/diversified-healthcare